ved_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-12-17T06:35:25Z","updated_at":"2025-12-17T20:02:08Z","closed_at":"2025-12-17T20:01:58Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: 4.5.1 Stable\nNot Reproducible in: When ResourceLoader did it (Sorry I was sick for the last year I do not know when this was changed).\n\n### System information\n\nMac OS 26.1 Godot 4.5.1 Stable (not CXX)\n\n### Issue description\n\nPreviously Resource Loader would load the root node of a GLTF file as a Node3D. \nNow with GLTFDocument the function\n`Node generate_scene(state: GLTFState, bake_fps: float = 30, trimming: bool = false, remove_immutable_tracks: bool = true)`\n\nI tried different Root Node Types but it always returns a Node instead of a Node3D. It seems like the value from a 3D file should be a Node3D type without needing to do a complicated maneuver? \n\nOr possibly add API to allow me to tell it to return a Node3D?\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCheck out documents here \n\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_gltfdocument.html#class-gltfdocument-method-append-from-file\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nShould just open a GLTF file.","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShip